\title{Exact equation}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2021-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{The ODE (#{\ast}) is \em{exact} if #{Q(x, y)\,dy + P(x, y)\,dx} is an \em{exact differential}, i.e. there exists #{f(x, y)} such that}

##{df = P(x, y)\,dx + Q(x, y)\,dy.}

\p{If (#{\ast}) is exact, #{df = 0 \Rightarrow f(x, y) = \text{constant}} is a solution.}
